      "math_academy_id": "q-348693",
      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t),\\,\\sqrt{t+3},\\,t-1⟩,$ what is $|r(1)|?$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$|r(1)|=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Evaluating the function at $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ),\\,\\sqrt{4},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,2,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(1)| & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
